153	\section{Assessment of Principal Drawback}
154	\label{sec:drawback}
155	The principal weakness of the paper is that \textbf{its grand synthesis relies almost entirely on classical, probe, and supergravity approximations, while the quantum consistency, equations of motion, and non-abelian field-theoretic structures of its proposals remain largely unverified}. 
156	Specifically, the framework faces three critical technical and conceptual obstacles:
157	\begin{enumerate}
158	    \item \textbf{Unverified Supergravity Equations of Motion and Torsional Constraints:}
159	    In constructing new non-Lorentzian holographic bulk geometries from off-aligned brane solutions ($p \neq q$), the authors must introduce an \emph{ad hoc} $\omega$-dependent rescaling of the characteristic length $\ell$ (or coordinate smearing) to prevent metric and form degeneracies. This corresponds to scaling the brane charge as $N \sim \omega^{(q-p)/2} \to \infty$. 
160	    Crucially, as acknowledged in the Outlook, \emph{the authors do not verify that the resulting non-Lorentzian backgrounds satisfy the equations of motion or the requisite supersymmetric torsional constraints of 10D/11D non-Lorentzian supergravity}. Without demonstrating that these backgrounds are legitimate dynamical extrema, their status as genuine holographic duals remains speculative.
