529	    \item \textbf{Holography as a $\text{DLCQ}^n/\text{DLCQ}^m$ Correspondence:} By uplifting these decoupling limits to M-theory, where each BPS decoupling limit lies in the U-duality orbit of a Discrete Light Cone Quantisation (DLCQ), the authors organise the landscape of holographic dualities into a $\text{DLCQ}^n/\text{DLCQ}^m$ ($m > n$) hierarchy. Standard single-stack holography ($\text{AdS}_5/\text{CFT}_4$ and IMSY) is identified as $\text{DLCQ}^0/\text{DLCQ}^1$, intersecting brane systems (such as D1-D5 $\text{AdS}_3/\text{CFT}_2$) as $\text{DLCQ}^0/\text{DLCQ}^2$, and consecutive ``off-aligned'' limits (applying an asymptotic M$p$T limit to a D$q$-brane background with $m+n=4$, followed by a near-horizon M$q$T limit) systematically generate $\text{DLCQ}^1/\text{DLCQ}^2$ non-Lorentzian holographic dualities.
