547	    \end{equation}
548	    where $\mathcal{T}^\alpha{}_\beta = \tau^{\alpha\gamma} T_{\gamma\beta}$ is the full stress-energy tensor (including gauge field contributions). This simple, polynomial, closed-form structure makes $p=2$ uniquely tractable among all higher-dimensional ($p \ge 1$) D-brane theories.
549	    \item \textbf{Two-Pronged Attack via Myers Action and 3D Superspace (Feasibility):} The problem can be attacked concretely in two complementary steps:
550	    \begin{enumerate}
551	        \item \emph{Non-Abelian D2-Brane Flow:} Starting from the Myers non-abelian D2-brane action reparametrised under the M2T scaling (Section~2.5.2, where $\boldsymbol{t} = \omega^{-2}$ controls both the kinetic determinant and the commutator potential $Q^i{}_j = \delta^i{}_j + i \boldsymbol{t}^{1/2} [X^i, X^k] E_{kj}$), one can compute the non-abelian stress-energy tensor $T_{\alpha\beta}(\boldsymbol{t})$ under the symmetrised trace prescription ($\text{STr}$) and determine whether Eq.~\eqref{eq:m2flow} holds exactly inside $\text{STr}$ or requires specific commutator-dependent corrections at order $\mathcal{O}(\boldsymbol{t})$.
552	        \item \emph{Supersymmetric Extension and ABJM/BLG:} Using established 3D superspace techniques for $T\bar{T}$-like flows (building on Ferko \emph{et al.}~\cite{Ferko:2023sps}), one can promote the operator in Eq.~\eqref{eq:m2flow} to a 3D supercurrent-squared operator. Because the Chern-Simons term in ABJM/BLG is topological, it does not contribute to the metric stress-energy tensor $T_{\alpha\beta}$, meaning the flow acts directly on the matter kinetic and sextic potential sectors.
553	    \end{enumerate}
554	    \item \textbf{High Impact on M-Theory and Non-Abelian DBI:} While the abelian DBI action for a single D-brane or M2-brane is well understood, a first-principles derivation of the non-abelian M2-brane action at finite $\boldsymbol{t}$ (deforming away from the non-relativistic M-theory / ABJM limit back toward relativistic M-theory) is a long-standing open problem in string/M-theory. Establishing how Eq.~\eqref{eq:m2flow} deforms 3D $\mathcal{N}=8$ SYM and ABJM/BLG would provide a systematic, symmetry-guided definition of the non-abelian relativistic membrane action, while simultaneously testing the paper's core thesis that $p$-brane $T\bar{T}$ deformations invert the DLCQ / BPS decoupling limit at the interacting, non-abelian level.
555	\end{itemize}
556	\begin{thebibliography}{9}
557	\bibitem{Ferko:2023sps}
558	C.~Ferko, Y.~Hu, Z.~Huang, K.~Koutrolikos, and G.~Tartaglino-Mazzucchelli, \emph{{$T \overline{T}$-like flows and $3d$ nonlinear supersymmetry}}, \emph{SciPost Phys.} \textbf{16} (2024) 038, [\texttt{arXiv:2302.10410}].
559	\end{thebibliography}
